    "F-357": {
      "title": "Bi-Lipschitz coordinates at every regular RCD point.",
      "subject": "Differential geometry",
      "catalogue_claim_unverified": "Proves that every regular point of a noncollapsed $`\\mathop{\\mathrm{RCD}}\\nolimits (K,n)`$ space, for <i>K</i> ∈ ℝ and integer <i>n</i> ≥ 2, has an open neighborhood bi-Lipschitz to an open subset of ℝ<sup><i>n</i></sup>. Regularity requires all pointed tangents to be Euclidean, the reference measure is exactly $`\\mathcal H^n`$, and the chart compares ambient distances with a point-dependent finite constant.",
